Count chartr()'s translation table in R_xlen_t and reject more
than INT_MAX entries.

do_chartr() (src/main/character.c) counts the expanded 'old' spec
into an int, xtable_cnt, before allocating the table with R_alloc()
and filling it in a second pass.  A spec whose ranges add up to 2^32
characters wraps the count to 0: R_alloc() hands back a one-entry
table and the fill loop writes 4G entries past it.  A valid 23 KB
spec of repeated "\x01-\U0010FFFF" ranges in a UTF-8 locale does it;
R 4.5.3 segfaults in about 7 s.  Count in R_xlen_t and signal an
error above INT_MAX, since the table is indexed with int below.

Found by OSS-Fuzz (libFuzzer_r_character, Timeout): testcase
5469970587516928 led to the review of the native-string path that
found this; the testcase itself is a 6-byte UTF-8 range that glibc's
mbstowcs() still decodes, handled by the harness guard.

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #458 and Bugzilla PR#19292, filed
2026-11-07.
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk.

diff --git a/src/main/character.c b/src/main/character.c
--- a/src/main/character.c
+++ b/src/main/character.c
@@ -1448,7 +1448,7 @@
     if (mbcslocale || use_WC == TRUE) {
 	int j, nb, nc;
 	xtable_t *xtable, *tbl;
-	int xtable_cnt;
+	R_xlen_t xtable_cnt;
 	struct wtr_spec *trs_cnt, **trs_cnt_ptr;
 	wchar_t c_old, c_new, *wc;
 	const char *xi, *s;
@@ -1523,6 +1523,10 @@
 	*trs_cnt_ptr = trs_cnt->next;
 	for (xtable_cnt = 0 ; wtr_get_next_char_from_spec(trs_cnt_ptr);
 	      xtable_cnt++) ;
+	/* the table is indexed with int below; counted in int, 2^32
+	   entries wrapped to 0 and the table was written past its end */
+	if (xtable_cnt > INT_MAX)
+	    error(_("'old' expands to too many characters"));
 	xtable = (xtable_t *) R_alloc(xtable_cnt+1, sizeof(xtable_t));
 
 	trs_old_ptr = (struct wtr_spec **) R_alloc(1, sizeof(struct wtr_spec *));
